Ticket #4471 merged every date report into one known issue. The reports are two problems. The table counts unique report ids. A repeated id in the export is one report.

## The two problems

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The cause marked as this ticket is the shared parser. It reads every date month-first, so a day-first tenant's day and month come out swapped.

The other cause is the booking-v3 form. The hint under its date field is `MM/DD/YYYY`. The form then reads the date the tenant's way, day first, so people type the month first and the form takes that as the day. Those reports were merged into #4471 and have no ticket of their own.

A few reports were read by the desk as a one-day move. They stay in the count of the cause their tenant files them under. The note under the table is that reading.

<Callout>
Each row is one problem. The report count on that row is how many reports the problem covers.
</Callout>

